# API layer types (controller → service)

Follow `ProductService` as the reference. Keep controller thin; service owns the use-case boundary.

## Roles

| Type | Package | Role |
|------|---------|------|
| `*Request` | `...request` | Input for a use-case (validation annotations). Create/Update/Filter are separate types. |
| `*Response` | `...response` | Output shaped for a specific endpoint/use-case (page wrapper, created id, etc.). |
| `*DTO` | `...dto` | Reusable read/nested shape (list item, nested objects inside Request/Response). |
| Entity | `...entity` | Persistence only — never expose from controller or as service return to API. |

## Rules

- **HTTP in** → `*Request`. Do not use `*DTO` as create/update body when it carries read-only/audit fields.
- **HTTP out** → `*Response` for use-case-specific payloads; nest `*DTO` for items/details when the shape is reusable.
- **List/page** → `*PageResponse extends PageResponse<*DTO>` (or equivalent). Never return a single `*DTO` from `getPage`.
- **Create** → `Create*Request` in, prefer `*CreatedResponse` or the read `*DTO` out.
- **Update** → `Update*Request` (or path id + request); do not reuse create request if fields differ.
- **Filter** → `*FilterRequest` / `*PageRequest` for query params.
- MapStruct (or mappers) convert Entity ↔ DTO/Request/Response inside the service layer.

## Good

```java
WarehousePageResponse getPage(WarehouseFilterRequest request, Pageable pageable);
WarehouseDTO getById(UUID id);
WarehouseDTO create(CreateWarehouseRequest request);
WarehouseDTO update(UUID id, UpdateWarehouseRequest request);
void delete(UUID id);
```

```java
// Page response wraps DTO items
public class WarehousePageResponse extends PageResponse<WarehouseDTO> {}
```

## Bad

```java
// DTO as create/update body when it includes id/audit fields clients must not send
WarehouseDTO create(WarehouseDTO warehouse);

// getPage returning a single DTO
WarehouseDTO getPage(WarehouseFilterRequest request, Pageable pageable);

// Entity leaked to controller
Warehouse create(...);
```
